# The compiled admin panel is a build artefact compared byte for byte by CI
# ("the committed bundle must match the source"). Line-ending conversion makes
# that comparison depend on which machine last ran `npm run build`: committed
# from Windows the blob carries CRLF, and the Linux runner's vite writes LF, so
# every line differs and the check reports a stale bundle that is in fact
# identical. `-text` stores exactly what the build produced, on any platform.
ui/dist/** -text

# The golden data_dir fixture is a byte-for-byte recording of on-disk formats.
# Line-ending normalization would rewrite the WAL segment and break its
# per-record checksums, so the whole tree is exempt from any text conversion —
# `-text` is what makes that guarantee, and `binary` also keeps diffs quiet.
tests/fixtures/golden_data_dir/** -text -diff
# Except its README, which is prose and should behave like every other doc.
tests/fixtures/golden_data_dir/README.md text
